<div class="row">
    <div class="col-lg-12 text-center">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-10 offset-lg-1">
                <h4>OctoFarm is the work of James Mackay (NotExpectedYet)</h4><hr>
                <p class="text-left">He designed it after using the wonderful software OctoPrint for well over a
                    year before getting his second printer. Realising he could only control and monitor one
                    printer from the OctoPrint interface, he decided to write his own implementation using
                    OctoPrint's API. That became OctoFarm, used for monitoring and managing multiple OctoPrint
                    attached printers.</p>
                <p class="text-left">Practically everything you are looking at is his: the printer management, the
                    monitoring views, the file and filament managers, the history system, and the OctoPrint API
                    and websocket layer underneath all of it. Years of that work were given away free and open
                    source under the AGPL, which is the only reason anything below exists. The credit for this
                    application belongs to James and to everyone who contributed to OctoFarm.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row mt-4">
            <div class="col-lg-10 offset-lg-1">
                <h4>What OctoFarm-Redux is</h4><hr>
                <p class="text-left">A redux of that original, maintained by DaniSim. Upstream development
                    stopped in 2023, so this version keeps it alive - and it has grown well past maintenance
                    since. The whole stack has been brought back to current, supported versions and a long list
                    of security holes and long-standing bugs closed.</p>
                <p class="text-left">It also adds a good deal upstream never had: a rebuilt file manager with
                    housekeeping mode, bulk delete, filtering by print outcome, an age-based sweep, thumbnail
                    previews and copying a file straight to other printers; spool numbers you can sticker onto
                    the physical roll; a pre-flight check that warns before a print the assigned spool cannot
                    finish; cancelling a single object from a running job, with a top-down plan of the bed;
                    farm-wide Maintenance Mode; a Torch button for the printer light; cameras streamed through
                    OctoFarm itself and recovering on their own; and cost tracking you can narrow down to
                    filament alone.</p>
                <p class="text-left">None of that replaces how OctoFarm works - it is still the application
                    James built, and this is no successor to it. The full list of changes is in the project's
                    README.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row mt-4">
            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6">
                <h4>Project</h4><hr>
                <p class="small">Bug reports and feature requests go through GitHub issues.</p>
                <a type="button" class="btn btn-light mb-2" href="<%= links.REPO_URL %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><i class="fab fa-github"></i> Repository</a><br>
                <a type="button" class="btn btn-info mb-2" href="<%= links.ISSUES_URL %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><i class="fas fa-bug"></i> Report an Issue</a><br>
                <a type="button" class="btn btn-warning dark-text" href="<%= links.README_URL %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Documentation</a>
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6">
                <h4>Support</h4><hr>
                <p class="small">OctoFarm-Redux is free. If it has been useful to you, there is a tip jar -
                    entirely optional, nothing is locked behind it. It supports maintenance of this fork only;
                    the original project's own donation links are long defunct.</p>
                <a type="button" class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= links.KOFI_URL %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><i class="fas fa-mug-hot"></i> Buy me a coffee on Ko-fi</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
